<!--
  MAINTAINER NOTES (all verified 2026-09-23)

  1. The ampersand in the Crimson Dining URL must be written as &amp; in this file.
     A bare & makes the file invalid XML: a strict parser stops at that line and
     silently drops every URL after it. Do NOT write it as %26 - that is
     percent-encoding, not XML escaping, and the site returns 404 for %26.

  2. The apostrophes in the-bear's-den and dunkin' are correct. They are the real
     slugs. Do not "clean them up": the-bears-den and dunkin both 404, and the
     percent-encoded %27 forms also 404. Leave them as literal apostrophes.

  3. Do NOT add /en-us/locations/hours or /en-us/locations/map. Both look ideal
     and both are client-rendered. Fetched without JavaScript they return a stale
     week with every location marked "Closed" and no times at all. A crawler would
     learn from them that campus dining is shut. The individual location pages
     below carry their hours in server-side HTML, which is why they are used here.

  4. No <lastmod> elements. lastmod means the date the PAGE last changed, which we
     do not know for a third-party site. Leaving it out is more honest than
     inventing one. The revision date above tracks this file instead.
-->
